    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with significant firepower at the top of the lineup, anchored by **Trea Turner** (79.76) and **Kyle Schwarber** (78.16). Both benefit immensely from a favorable encounter with Mor\u00e1n, as the positive park factors and elite lineup positioning for both hitters elevate them to our strongest plays of the day. **Junior Caminero** (73.89) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (74.66) also grade out as elite options; **Crow-Armstrong** specifically benefits from a massive 14% platoon boost against Grant Holmes, making him a critical start as we hunt for stolen bases to maintain our competitive edge in the category. \n\nWhile **Luke Raley** (60.45) provides a solid start thanks to an inviting matchup against Tatsuya Imai\u2019s high expected ERA, our most difficult bench decision involved **Casey Schmitt** (46.16). Despite a solid individual score, **Schmitt** was pushed out of the lineup primarily because he is facing an elite arm in Yoshinobu Yamamoto, whose SP skill significantly dampened his efficiency. The optimizer favored the floor of **Chase Meidroth** (50.86) and the specific matchup advantages held by our outfield starters. We continue to monitor the status of **Gary Sanchez**, whose status remains \"Lineup Pending\"; should he move down from his assumed #4 spot, his efficiency score of 40.17 could dip below our floor, forcing a late-day re-evaluation of the catcher slot. We remain cautious with **Caleb Durbin** on the bench today, as his matchup against Zack Wheeler poses too much risk for a high-leverage category day.",
